{
  "id": "Its_Patch_Tuesday_for_Microsoft_Not_a_Zero_Day_In_Sight_txt_8",
  "content": "The two Microsoft Office Word vulnerabilities in Microsoft's latest update with the preview pane attack vector are CVE-2026-40361 (CVSS 8.4) and CVE-2026-40364 (CVSS 8.4). The former is a memory-related vulnerability that allows a remote attacker to execute code locally on vulnerable systems. CVE-2026-40464 too is a remote code execution (RCE) bug stemming from a type-confusion issue. Neither vulnerability requires any user interaction. An attacker can trigger the flaws by simply sending a maliciously crafted document. \"Outlook's reading pane has long been a common attack vector; a single incoming email can trigger exploitation without the user ever opening it,\" warned Amol Sarwate, head of security research at Cohesity, in a statement.",
  "category": "Article",
  "source": "Local Storage",
